## Why This Is Asked

Car environments introduce dynamic geometry, intermittent sensor faults, and real-time constraints. This question probes the ability to design an online ICA solution that adapts to changing mixing, handles missing data gracefully, and maintains consistent source order over time.

## Key Concepts

- Online sliding-window ICA with adaptive whitening
- Kalman-style demixer updates on whitened data
- Missing-channel handling via subspace completion without reinitialization
- Permutation stability using short temporal memory and cross-frame non-Gaussianity cues
- Real-time latency targets and robust evaluation (ground-truth SDR/SIR, perceptual checks)

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: online update for W on whitened data Xw
function onlineUpdate(W, Xw, lr) {
  const Y = W.dot(Xw);
  const e = gradientNonGaussianity(Y);
  return W.add(e.mul(lr).dot(Xw.transpose()));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you diagnose instability when sources cross or when dropouts occur?
- How would you scale to larger arrays with nonuniform sampling or asynchronous microphones?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design real-time blind source separation systems for mobile platforms with dynamic geometry and environmental noise challenges, emphasizing adaptive signal processing, cross-bin coherence, and multimodal self-supervised learning approaches.

## Key Concepts

- Geometry-aware whitening with adaptive tracking
- Online ICA versus joint diagonalization strategies
- Dynamic demixer scaling and computational cadence
- Cross-bin permutation alignment using envelope analysis
- Video-driven self-supervised permutation stabilization

## Code Example

```javascript
// Geometry-aware online whitening with forgetting factor
function geometryAwareWhitening(micSignals, forgettingFactor = 0.95) {
  const covariance = updateCovariance(micSignals, forgettingFactor);
  const whiteningMatrix = computeWhiteningMatrix(covariance);
  return applyWhitening(micSignals, whiteningMatrix);
}

// Adaptive switching between per-bin ICA and joint diagonalization
function selectICAStrategy(signalQuality, frequencyBins) {
  if (signalQuality > THRESHOLD_HIGH) {
    return 'jointDiagonalization';
  } else if (signalQuality > THRESHOLD_LOW) {
    return 'perBinICA';
  }
  return 'hybridApproach';
}

// Cross-bin permutation alignment using envelope correlation
function alignPermutations(separatedSources, sampleRate) {
  const envelopes = computeEnvelopes(separatedSources);
  const correlationMatrix = computeEnvelopeCorrelation(envelopes);
  return resolvePermutationAmbiguity(correlationMatrix);
}

// Self-supervised loss using synchronized video
function videoGuidedLoss(audioSources, videoFeatures) {
  const audioVisualCorrelation = computeCrossModalCorrelation(audioSources, videoFeatures);
  return -audioVisualCorrelation.mean(); // Minimize negative correlation
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
The prompt probes distributed ICA, privacy, and real-time constraints across heterogeneous devices.

## Key Concepts
- Decentralized online convolutive ICA, masked statistics, cross-device permutation alignment.
- Dropout resilience, privacy-preserving aggregation, on-device evaluation.
- Time-varying mixing, latency budgets, evaluation with ground-truth sources.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: local whitening + ICA + masked share
function localICA(X) {
  const W = whiten(X);
  const S = fastICA(W);
  return S;
}
```

